analysisWe need to write assert statement for comment.

We have method add(int index, Attribute attribute). It adds attribute at index, shifting existing elements right. The comment: "If the index is within the valid range (from 0 to the initial size of the list), then for every position from the index to the old size of the list, the element at each position plus one is either both null or equal to the element at that position before the addition."

Interpretation: For all positions i such that index <= i < oldSize (old size before addition), after addition, element at position i+1 is either both null (i.e., both old element at i and new element at i+1 are null) or equal (i.e., new element at i+1 equals old element at i). Since we are dealing with Attributes, we can use .equals for equality? In previous examples they used .equals for objects. Use this.get(i) returns Attribute. So we need to refer to old list element: \old(this.get(i)). After addition, new element at i+1 is this.get(i+1). Condition: (this.get(i+1)==null && \old(this.get(i))==null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))) . But need to handle null safely; we can express as (this.get(i+1) == null ? \old(this.get(i)) == null : this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) . However examples used "either both null or equal". They wrote "this.query(i).equals(\old(this.query(i)))" for equality; they didn't handle null. For null case they used "both null or equal". We can express using " (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)))". That's fine.

Premise: index is within valid range: 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()). The comment says "from 0 to the initial size of the list". Since after addition size becomes oldSize+1. So condition: index >=0 && index <= \old(this.size()). Also note that if index is invalid, exception thrown, but we only assert for valid case. So we assert: (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); ( (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))) );

Need to use proper syntax: \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); ( (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))) )

Wrap with implication.

Thus final assert:

assert (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); ( (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))) );

Make sure parentheses around forall spec? Use syntax: \forall int i; cond; spec . So we need: \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); ( (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))) )

All good.

